{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-210760",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 3,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ {\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{x}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{1-t/3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-t/3}{|}_{3}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-x/3}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{1-x/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3, \\\\ 1-{e}^{1-x/3}, & x\\ge 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
